    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379">

                <pb facs="0825" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President,
                        and Reply by the President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d379-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yalta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-02-07">February 7, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>All of the below refers to Churchill’s opposition to early calling of conference
                    of United Nations.</p>
                <p>There is something behind this talk that we do not know of its basis.</p>
                <p>Perhaps we better to wait till later tonight what is on his mind.</p>
                <p>All this is <del rendition="#strikethrough">rot</del>! local politics<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d379-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am quite sure now he is thinking about the next election in Britain.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d379-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d379-f1-content">
                <p>The relationship of these notes to the Fourth Plenary Meeting appears from
                    internal evidence and from Sherwood, pp. 862–864. See <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg714">p. 714</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d379-f2" n="2" xml:id="d379-f2-content">
                <p>This line is in Roosevelt’s handwriting.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
